## 2.1 Frontend Stack

### Framework
- React 18+ with Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- TypeScript (strict mode, 100% type coverage)
- SSR + SSG for marketing/SEO pages
- ISR for product catalog pages
- Streaming SSR for dashboard pages

### State Management
- Zustand for global UI state (theme, language, sidebar, notifications)
- TanStack Query (React Query v5) for server state (all API data, caching, mutations, optimistic updates)
- React Context for auth/session context only
- URL state via Next.js searchParams for filters/sorting/pagination

### Styling
- Tailwind CSS v3.4+ (with JIT, custom config, dark mode via class strategy)
- CSS Modules for component-scoped styles where needed
- CSS Custom Properties for all design tokens (colors, spacing, radius, shadows, transitions, z-index, fonts)
- @layer directives: base, components, utilities
- No inline styles except for dynamic values from JS
- Logical CSS properties (margin-inline, padding-block, inset-inline-start) for RTL/LTR

### UI Component Library
- Radix UI primitives (accessible, unstyled) as foundation
- Custom design system built on Radix (not a pre-made library)
- Shadcn/UI pattern: own the components, copy and customize
- Framer Motion for animations and page transitions
- Lucide React for icons (consistent stroke width, tree-shakeable)
- Recharts for data visualization (charts, graphs)
- React Hook Form + Zod for form handling and validation
- TanStack Table for data tables (sorting, filtering, pagination, virtualization)
- Sonner for toast notifications
- Cmdk for command palette

### Internationalization (i18n)
- next-intl or next-i18next for multi-language support
- Languages: Arabic (ar), French (fr), English (en) at launch
- RTL support: automatic direction switching based on locale
- All user-facing strings in translation files (JSON)
- Date/time formatting withIntl.DateTimeFormat
- Number formatting with Intl.NumberFormat
- Currency formatting per locale
- Language switcher in header (no page reload)

### PWA
- next-pwa for service worker generation
- Web manifest with app icons, theme color, display standalone
- Offline fallback page
- Push notification support (web-push API)
- Install prompt handling

### Key Frontend Libraries
next, react, react-dom typescript, @types/react, @types/node tailwindcss, postcss, autoprefixer framer-motion zustand @tanstack/react-query, @tanstack/react-table react-hook-form, zod, @hookform/resolvers @radix-ui/react-* (all primitives) lucide-react recharts react-hook-form sonner cmdk next-intl next-pwa date-fns clsx, tailwind-merge



## 2.2 Backend Stack

### Framework
- Node.js 20+ LTS
- NestJS 10+ (modular monolithic architecture)
- TypeScript (strict mode, shared types with frontend)
- Fastify adapter (instead of Express) for performance

### Architecture Pattern
- Modular Monolithic (feature-based modules)
- Each feature is a self-contained module: controller, service, repository, dto, entity
- Dependency Injection via NestJS DI container
- Modules: Auth, Users, Tenants, Products, Orders, Customers, Campaigns, Content, Analytics, Automation, Integrations, Billing, Notifications, Files, Agents, Reports
- Inter-module communication via events (EventEmitter) and direct service injection
- Future path: extract modules into microservices when scale demands

### API Design
- REST API (primary) with OpenAPI/Swagger documentation
- GraphQL API (secondary) for flexible client queries
- API versioning: /api/v1/...
- Rate limiting: per-IP and per-tenant
- Request validation with class-validator + class-transformer
- Response serialization with class-transformer (exclude sensitive fields)
- Pagination: cursor-based for large datasets, offset for small
- Error handling: global exception filter with structured error responses
- Health checks: /api/health, /api/health/ready, /api/health/live

### Authentication & Authorization
- JWT-based authentication (access token + refresh token)
- Access token: 15min expiry, stored in httpOnly secure cookie
- Refresh token: 7-day expiry, stored in httpOnly secure cookie, rotated on use
- Session management: Redis-backed session store
- Password hashing: bcrypt with salt rounds 12
- 2FA: TOTP-based (Google Authenticator compatible) with backup codes
- OAuth: Google, Facebook social login (optional)
- RBAC: role-based access control with custom roles
  - Owner: full access + billing + security
  - Admin: everything except billing
  - Manager: module-specific management
  - Staff: assigned module access with CRUD limits
  - Accountant: financial views only
  - Support: customer/ticket views only
  - Agent: AI agent role with scoped permissions
  - Partner: limited partner portal access
  - Customer: customer portal access
- Permission granularity: per-module, per-action (create, read, update, delete, approve, export)
- Multi-tenant isolation: every query scoped by tenant_id

### Key Backend Libraries
@nestjs/core, @nestjs/common, @nestjs/platform-fastify @nestjs/config, @nestjs/jwt, @nestjs/passport @nestjs/typeorm, @nestjs/swagger @nestjs/event-emitter class-validator, class-transformer bcrypt, otplib, qrcode ioredis, @nestjs/bull, bull @nestjs/schedule handlebars (email templates)



## 2.3 Database Architecture

### Primary Database
- PostgreSQL 16+ (primary relational database)
- ORM: TypeORM or Prisma (choose Prisma for type safety and migration safety)
- Connection pooling via PgBouncer or Prisma connection pool
- Multi-tenant strategy: shared database, shared schema, tenant_id column on every table
  - Row-level security policies for tenant isolation
  - All queries automatically filtered by tenant context
  - Tenant context injected via middleware/interceptor

### Caching
- Redis 7+ for:
  - Session storage
  - Token blacklisting
  - Rate limiting counters
  - Real-time presence (online status)
  - Job queues (Bull)
  - Feature flags
  - Hot data caching (product catalogs, dashboards)
  - Pub/Sub for real-time events

### Search
- Elasticsearch 8+ or Meilisearch for:
  - Product search (full-text, fuzzy, faceted)
  - Customer search
  - Order search
  - Log/analytics search
  - Auto-complete suggestions

### Time-Series (Future)
- ClickHouse or TimescaleDB for:
  - Analytics aggregation
  - Event tracking
  - Large-scale reporting

### File Storage
- MinIO (S3-compatible) or AWS S3 for:
  - Product images
  - User avatars
  - Document uploads
  - Export files
  - Public CDN assets

