## 2.4 Multi-Tenancy Architecture

### Strategy
- Shared database with tenant_id column on every table
- Row-Level Security (RLS) policies in PostgreSQL
- Tenant context resolver middleware: extracts tenant_id from JWT or subdomain
- All repository queries automatically filter by tenant_id
- Tenant isolation interceptor: rejects cross-tenant access
- Per-tenant configuration table (features, limits, branding)
- Per-tenant rate limiting and quota enforcement

### Tenant Lifecycle
- Provisioning: create tenant record, default config, seed data
- Active: full access
- Suspended: read-only + billing prompts
- Cancelled: grace period then data retention then deletion

