Common Automations (Pre-built)
New order → email confirmation + update inventory + notify shipping + update CRM
New customer → welcome email + add to CRM + assign segment + schedule follow-up
Abandoned cart → reminder email after 1h + SMS after 24h + discount after 72h
Low stock → alert manager + suggest reorder + update product status
Low-performing campaign → alert + suggest changes + pause if below threshold
Customer birthday → send reward + personalized email
Win-back campaign → detect churn risk + send re-engagement sequence
4.7 AI Agents Module
Agent Types (Build Each as a Functional Service)
Agent 1: Audience Analyst
Analyzes customer behavior data (purchases, browsing, engagement)
Segments customers automatically (RFM analysis, behavioral clustering)
Identifies high-value segments, at-risk segments, growth segments
Generates audience insights reports
Feeds segment data to Campaign Builder agent
API: POST /api/v1/agents/audience/analyze
Agent 2: Campaign Builder
Creates campaign structures based on goals and audience data
Suggests budget allocation across channels
Recommends ad creative variations
Sets up A/B tests automatically
Monitors campaign performance and suggests optimizations
Can auto-pause underperforming campaigns
API: POST /api/v1/agents/campaigns/build
Agent 3: Content Generator
Generates marketing copy (ad headlines, descriptions, email subject lines, body content)
Generates product descriptions from product data
Generates social media posts
Generates SEO content (meta descriptions, blog outlines)
Supports multiple languages (ar, fr, en)
Learns from user edits and preferences
API: POST /api/v1/agents/content/generate
Agent 4: Product Recommender
Analyzes customer purchase history and browsing behavior
Generates personalized product recommendations
Creates "frequently bought together" bundles
Identifies cross-sell and upsell opportunities
Powers on-site recommendation widgets
API: POST /api/v1/agents/recommend
Agent 5: Customer Manager
Monitors customer health scores
Predicts churn risk (based on engagement decline, support tickets, order frequency)
Triggers win-back automations
Manages customer segmentation updates
Suggests personalized communication
API: POST /api/v1/agents/customers/manage
Agent 6: Decision Support
Analyzes overall business performance
Identifies trends, anomalies, opportunities
Generates executive summaries and recommendations
Provides what-if analysis (e.g., "What if you increase ad spend by 20%?")
Suggests strategic actions with predicted impact
API: POST /api/v1/agents/decision/analyze
Agent 7: Automation Orchestrator
Coordinates all other agents
Manages agent task queues and priorities
Resolves conflicts between agent recommendations
Learns from user acceptance/rejection of suggestions
Schedules regular analysis runs
API: POST /api/v1/agents/orchestrator/run
Agent Architecture
Each agent is a NestJS service module
Agents communicate via internal event bus
Each agent has a task queue (Bull queue + Redis)
Agent tasks are async with progress tracking
Agent results stored in agent_tasks and agent_logs tables
User can configure agent autonomy level: suggest-only, auto-execute-with-approval, full-auto
Agent dashboard showing recent agent activities and suggestions
Agent settings per tenant (enable/disable, autonomy level, frequency)
AI Integration
OpenAI API (GPT-4 Turbo) for text generation and analysis
Or local LLM (Ollama) for cost-sensitive deployments
Embedding model for semantic search (OpenAI embeddings or local model)
Vector database (pgvector or Pinecone) for similarity search
Prompt templates stored in database (per-agent, per-language)
Rate limiting and cost tracking per tenant
