PART 7 — SECURITY REQUIREMENTS
═══════════════════════════════════════
7.1 Authentication Security
bcrypt password hashing (salt rounds 12)
JWT access tokens (15min) + refresh tokens (7 days, rotated)
httpOnly + secure + sameSite cookies
2FA (TOTP) with backup codes
Rate limiting: 5 login attempts per 15min per IP
Account lockout: 5 failed attempts → 30min lock
Session invalidation on password change
Password breach check (haveibeenpwned API or similar)
7.2 Data Security
TLS 1.3 for all connections
AES-256 encryption at rest (database)
Sensitive data encryption (API keys, payment credentials)
PII data minimization and pseudonymization where possible
Data retention policies (configurable per tenant)
Secure data deletion (GDPR right to be forgotten)
7.3 Application Security
Input validation on all endpoints (class-validator)
Output encoding to prevent XSS
SQL injection prevention (parameterized queries via ORM)
CSRF protection (sameSite cookies + CSRF tokens for state-changing requests)
Content Security Policy headers
Security headers: X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, X-XSS-Protection, Referrer-Policy
CORS configuration (allowlist origins)
File upload validation (type, size, content)
Rate limiting on all API endpoints
Request size limiting
7.4 Audit & Compliance
Comprehensive audit logging (who, what, when, where)
Audit log retention: 90 days (standard), 1 year (Enterprise)
Audit log export (CSV, PDF)
GDPR compliance: data export, data deletion, consent management
Data processing agreements (DPA) support
Incident response plan
═══════════════════════════════════════
PART 8 — PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS
═══════════════════════════════════════
8.1 Frontend Performance
Lighthouse score: 90+ on all metrics (Performance, Accessibility, Best Practices, SEO)
First Contentful Paint: < 1.5s
Largest Contentful Paint: < 2.5s
Time to Interactive: < 3.5s
Cumulative Layout Shift: < 0.1
Total Blocking Time: < 200ms
Bundle size: < 200KB initial (gzipped)
Code splitting: per-route, per-module
Lazy loading: below-the-fold images, heavy components
Image optimization: WebP, responsive srcset, lazy loading
Font loading: font-display swap, preconnect, preload critical fonts
8.2 Backend Performance
API response time: < 200ms for 95% of requests
Database query time: < 50ms for 95% of queries
Connection pooling ( PgBouncer or Prisma pool)
Query optimization (indexes, N+1 elimination, eager loading)
Caching strategy: Redis for hot data, HTTP caching headers, ETags
Background jobs for heavy operations (email sending, report generation, imports)
Pagination: cursor-based for large datasets
Rate limiting: 100 req/min per tenant (adjustable per plan)
8.3 Real-Time
WebSocket connection for live updates (new orders, notifications, agent activities)
Fallback to polling if WebSocket unavailable
Efficient event broadcasting (only to relevant tenants/users)
